{{!< default}}

{{!-- The designed 404. Ghost resolves error-404.hbs ahead of error.hbs for a missing URL, so this
is the Surface a visitor actually reaches; error.hbs still covers every other status code.

The layout picker is `@custom.page_hero`, the same select About and Membership read: a buyer who
asked for a centred statement gets one here too. One {{#match}} at the top, the non-default option
matched explicitly so an unrecognised stored value falls through to a layout rather than to
nothing.

THIS SURFACE CANNOT BE PREVIEWED, ONLY VISITED. Ghost has no route that renders an error template
on request — an error page is what the router falls through to — so the capture set points at a
URL that genuinely does not exist and asserts a 404 status alongside the marker. A hand-made
preview route would have proved that the markup compiles and nothing about what a reader sees.

`{{#is}}` cannot match here either: an error page has no context at all, which is why every
Surface in this theme names its own chrome rather than deriving it. The foot is the slim one,
because a four-column footer under an apology outweighs it, and `<body>` is a flex column so the
message centres in whatever space is left and the foot sits on the bottom edge. --}}

{{> "chrome/header"}}

<main
	id="main"
	class="flex grow items-center"
	data-surface="error-404"
	data-layout="{{#match @custom.page_hero "Split hero"}}Split hero{{else}}Centered statement{{/match}}">

	{{#match @custom.page_hero "Split hero"}}
		{{> "error/a2"}}
	{{else}}
		{{> "error/a1"}}
	{{/match}}

</main>

{{> "chrome/footer" slim=true}}
